.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-PGP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-pgp
.Nd OpenPGP keys, signatures and encrypted messages
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis pgp
.Cm keygen
.Fl n Ar user-id
.Op Fl a Ar alg
.Op Fl -sign-only
.Op Fl -pass-fd Ar n | Fl -pass-env Ar name
.Fl o Ar key
.Op Fl -force
.Nm noqtis pgp
.Cm show
.Ar key
.Nm noqtis pgp
.Cm sign
.Fl k Ar key
.Op Fl -detached | Fl -clear
.Op Fl -binary
.Op Fl -pass-fd Ar n | Fl -pass-env Ar name
.Op Fl o Ar out
.Op Fl -force
.Ar file
.Nm noqtis pgp
.Cm verify
.Fl -cert Ar cert
.Op Fl -content Ar file
.Op Fl o Ar out
.Op Fl -force
.Ar file
.Nm noqtis pgp
.Cm encrypt
.Op Fl -to Ar cert ...
.Op Fl -symmetric
.Op Fl k Ar key
.Op Fl -binary
.Op Fl -pass-fd Ar n | Fl -pass-env Ar name
.Op Fl o Ar out
.Op Fl -force
.Ar file
.Nm noqtis pgp
.Cm decrypt
.Fl k Ar key | Fl -symmetric
.Op Fl -cert Ar cert
.Op Fl -pass-fd Ar n | Fl -pass-env Ar name
.Op Fl o Ar out
.Op Fl -force
.Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis pgp
writes and reads OpenPGP (RFC 9580) in its version 6 forms, with
Ed25519 and X25519 of that RFC and the post-quantum algorithms of
RFC 9980 (published from draft-ietf-openpgp-pqc): ML-DSA-65 with
Ed25519, ML-KEM-768 with X25519, and SLH-DSA-SHAKE.
What it writes is ASCII armor unless
.Fl -binary
is given; what it reads may be either.
.Bl -tag -width "encrypt"
.It Cm keygen
Make a key for
.Ar user-id ,
by convention
.Dq Name <address> :
the secret key in
.Ar key
and its certificate, to give to others, in
.Ar key Ns Pa .pub .
.Fl a
names the algorithm of the primary key, which certifies and signs:
.Cm mldsa65-ed25519
(the default),
.Cm ed25519 ,
.Cm slh-shake-128s ,
.Cm slh-shake-128f
or
.Cm slh-shake-256s .
The key has an encryption subkey, ML-KEM-768 with X25519 (X25519 for
an
.Cm ed25519
key), unless
.Fl -sign-only
is given.
With a passphrase the secret key is kept under it (Argon2id, AES-256
with OCB).
An OpenPGP key is made here: the key files of
.Xr noqtis-keygen 1
are of another form and cannot be turned into one.
.It Cm show
Print what a key or a certificate says: its user ID, algorithms,
fingerprints and times.
.It Cm sign
Sign
.Ar file
with the secret key: a signed message that carries the data, with
.Fl -detached
the signature alone, with
.Fl -clear
the text itself with the signature under it (the file must be UTF-8
text).
.It Cm verify
Check a signed message, a cleartext signature, or a detached signature
of the file given with
.Fl -content ,
under the certificate
.Ar cert .
.Fl o
writes the data that was signed.
.It Cm encrypt
Encrypt
.Ar file
to the encryption subkeys of the certificates given with
.Fl -to
(up to 32), and with
.Fl -symmetric
to the passphrase as well, or alone: AES-256 with OCB.
.Fl k
signs the message first, inside the encryption.
With
.Fl -symmetric
the passphrase is that of the message, and
.Ar key
must then not be under one.
.It Cm decrypt
Open a message with the secret key
.Ar key ,
or with
.Fl -symmetric
with its passphrase.
With
.Fl -cert
the message must be signed by that certificate; without, the content
is written whatever signs it.
.El
.Pp
A passphrase is read from the descriptor of
.Fl -pass-fd
or the variable of
.Fl -pass-env ,
never from the command line.
.Fl -force
replaces an output that exists.
A file is created with mode 0644 whatever the umask; the secret key
.Ar key
of
.Cm keygen
and the output of
.Cm decrypt
are owner-only (mode 0600).
.Pp
Keys, signatures and messages of versions 3 and 4, RSA, DSA, Elgamal,
the NIST and Brainpool curves, CFB encryption and compressed data are
not supported, and are reported as such.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success;
1 when
.Cm verify
finds that a signature does not verify, and when
.Cm show
finds a key with no valid self-signature;
2 on a usage or file error, and when a message does not open.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
$ noqtis pgp keygen -n "Ada Example <ada@example.org>" -o ada
$ noqtis pgp sign -k ada --detached -o report.pdf.asc report.pdf
$ noqtis pgp verify --cert ada.pub --content report.pdf report.pdf.asc
OK, signed by Ada Example <ada@example.org> (...) at ...
$ noqtis pgp encrypt --to bob.pub -k ada -o secret.asc report.pdf
$ noqtis pgp decrypt -k bob --cert ada.pub -o report.pdf secret.asc
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-keygen 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-smime 1 ,
.Xr nqpgpgen 3
